# PCA from Scratch: Rwanda Food Prices (Formative 1)

Principal Component Analysis written from scratch with NumPy only (Matplotlib for plots), applied to WFP retail food prices from Rwandan markets, 2018–2026.

**Team:** Gatete Derrick, Abdul Kudus Zakaria Mukhtaru | **Peer pair:** 22

## Files

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `PCA_Formative_1_Rwanda_Food_Prices.ipynb` | Completed notebook with all outputs |
| `wfp_food_prices_rwa.csv` | Raw WFP dataset as downloaded (157,754 rows × 16 columns). The notebook reshapes it to 1,875 market-months × 13 columns with 1,596 missing values |
| `Task Sheet _Advanced Linear Algebra_Formative 2 - Principle Component Analysis_Cohort 2_Team22.pdf` | Task/contribution sheet |
| `Combined_Advanced Linear Algebra_Formative_2_ PCA_And_Team_Task_Sheet_Cohort 2_Team22.pdf` | Combined PDF (notebook + contribution sheet) |

## Data source

World Food Programme, Rwanda – Food Prices, Humanitarian Data Exchange: [https://data.humdata.org/dataset/wfp-food-prices-for-rwanda](https://data.humdata.org/dataset/wfp-food-prices-for-rwanda)

## Run it

Open the notebook in Google Colab (File → Open notebook → GitHub → paste this repo's URL), then Runtime → Run all. If the CSV isn't found, set `DATA_PATH` to this file's raw GitHub URL.

**Additional instructions:**
1. Make sure to display outputs for each code cell when submitting.
2. Do not write all your code on one cell.
3. Do not use any libraries aside from numpy (matplotlib is used only for plots).